From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:36:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] prj.conf: MP_NUM_CPUS -> MP_MAX_NUM_CPUS for Zephyr 4.x


CONFIG_MP_NUM_CPUS was already deprecated in Zephyr 3.6 (kernel/Kconfig
defined it as `default MP_MAX_NUM_CPUS`, so the assignment here never did
anything on its own) and was removed outright in 4.0, see
doc/releases/migration-guide-4.0.rst. Zephyr 4.x turns Kconfig warnings into
errors (scripts/kconfig/kconfig.py), so an assignment to a now-undefined
symbol fails the build rather than being ignored.

The value is unchanged: the 3.6 build's .config already had both
CONFIG_MP_NUM_CPUS=1 and CONFIG_MP_MAX_NUM_CPUS=1.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5[1m]
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending [xen-troops/zephyr-dom0-xt]
---
diff --git a/prj.conf b/prj.conf
index 569941c..4f9d242 100644
--- a/prj.conf
+++ b/prj.conf
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-CONFIG_MP_NUM_CPUS=1
+CONFIG_MP_MAX_NUM_CPUS=1
 CONFIG_XEN_STORE_SRV=y
 CONFIG_XEN_DOMAIN_MANAGEMENT=y
 CONFIG_XEN_SHELL=y
